        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Enda Kenny, Leo Varadkar, Simon Coveney\n- Organizations: Fine Gael\n- Events: 2017 Fine Gael leadership election\n- Roles: party leader, Deputy Leader of Fine Gael, Minister for Foreign Affairs and Trade\n\nFacts:\n- Simon Coveney was born on 16 June 1972.\n- The 2017 Fine Gael leadership election was triggered in May 2017 when Enda Kenny resigned as leader of Fine Gael.\n- On 2 June 2017, Leo Varadkar won the 2017 Fine Gael leadership election, defeating Simon Coveney by 60% to 40%.\n- Since June 2017, Simon Coveney has served as Deputy Leader of Fine Gael and as Minister for Foreign Affairs and Trade.",
